From b9feb77296961e3bf259086d14bf2befaa7683fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 16:06:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09069/11362] Add a lint that checks a verdict against its own
 rows; most artifacts have no rows to check

REQ-OPS-VERDICT-ROW-6261, answering "how do we make this process self improving?"
grounded in what actually failed this session rather than in general principle.

THE GAP. Existing checks test an artifact against ITSELF -- gate self-reports,
fabrication patterns, determination preservation, freshness. None asked whether
the headline is supported by the ROWS. Three artifacts in two days had headlines
their own rows contradicted: exp6252 reported gate-met while its ablation was
byte-identical to the baseline on 20 of 25 rows; exp6251 reported gate-met on 1
win, 1 loss and 2 rows pinned at floor/ceiling; exp6254 would have reported a
clean null while every row was None. Each was caught by a human reading rows,
which is not a process -- and it compounds, because the conductor plans from
honest_verdict.

Five checks, each built from one of those incidents. Advisory by default with one
hard class (ALL_ROWS_NULL); a hard block on fuzzy matching over free-form
artifacts is how a guard starts punishing one author for another's data.

IT HIT ITS OWN BUG CLASS TWICE WHILE BEING BUILT. The first version scanned only
top-level row keys and found nothing on exp6252, whose arms are nested -- a pattern
narrower than its concept, in the tool written to catch that. And _metric_like
excluded any field containing "_n", discarding best_of_n_held, exp6251's headline
metric; same unanchored-substring bug as "meta" inside "meta_tensor" in the
TAUTOLOGY check. Both fixed and both pinned by tests.

THE MORE IMPORTANT FINDING, surfaced by running it. Over the 60 most recent
artifacts it checks 3 and skips 57 -- and its first version printed a bare "OK"
while doing so, the guard-is-green-while-blind state this project keeps finding
elsewhere. Coverage is now always printed. The skips are mostly CORRECT: those
artifacts have no per-unit rows, only MODEL_SPECS, receipts and gate tallies.

So the real conclusion is bigger than the lint: most recent artifacts report a
verdict and aggregate numbers with no per-unit rows, making their headline claims
unfalsifiable from the artifact alone. No tool can check a claim whose evidence was
never written down. Per-unit rows should become a REQUIRED ARTIFACT FIELD for any
comparative claim, the way random_seed already is -- a planner-side convention
change, and the higher-leverage half of the answer.

